{"step_index":243,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-23T16:36:28Z","model":"gemini-3.8-flash-high","input_tokens":2592,"cache_read_tokens":115561,"output_tokens":2682,"content":"### Stockfish Chess Arena — Implementation Complete\n\n**Stockfish Chess Arena** is a fully functional, high-performance chess application powered by the real **Stockfish WebAssembly** chess engine running in a dedicated Web Worker.\n\n---\n\n### Key Architectural & Engine Highlights\n\n#### 1. WebAssembly Engine & Web Worker Architecture\n* **Non-Blocking Background Worker**: The Stockfish WASM engine runs completely inside a dedicated Web Worker (`/stockfish.js` & `/stockfish.wasm`), ensuring that deep alpha-beta search calculations never freeze the main thread or degrade UI frame rates.\n* **Standard UCI Protocol Implementation**:\n  * **Engine Handshake**: Sends `uci` and listens for `uciok`, then verifies with `isready` / `readyok`.\n  * **New Game Initialization**: Issues `ucinewgame` before every fresh match.\n  * **Position Dispatch**: Formats current board state as FEN strings via `position fen <FEN>`.\n  * **Search Execution**: Issues `go depth <N> movetime <MS>`.\n  * **Engine Preemption**: Sends `stop` or terminates the worker cleanly if the user resets the game or requests an undo while the engine is thinking.\n* **Safety Watchdog**: A configurable timeout safeguard triggers `stop` if search limits are exceeded, ensuring the UI is never left in an unhandled pending state.\n\n#### 2. Difficulty Scaling & Search Configuration\n| Difficulty | Search Depth | UCI Skill Level | Move Time | Playing Profile |\n| :--- | :---: | :---: | :---: | :--- |\n| **Beginner** | 3 plies | Level 2 | ~600 ms | Casual, fast moves; occasional tactical slips |\n| **Easy** | 6 plies | Level 7 | ~1,000 ms | Solid opening principles; moderate search |\n| **Medium** | 10 plies | Level 13 | ~1,500 ms | Club-level tactical awareness |\n| **Hard** | 14 plies | Level 18 | ~2,200 ms | Sharp tactical calculation and positional depth |\n| **Expert** | 18 plies | Level 20 | ~3,500 ms | Full Stockfish skill level & maximum depth |\n| **Custom** | 1–20 plies | 0–20 | 200–5,000 ms | Fine-tuned depth and thinking time sliders |\n\n---\n\n### Core UI/UX & Functional Features\n\n* **Centered Responsive Board**: Built with `react-chessboard` featuring custom dark slate/charcoal styling (`#2b3648` dark squares, `#576a85` light squares) with subtle cyan ambient glow.\n* **Visual Square Indicators**:\n  * **Selected Square**: Glowing cyan highlight (`rgba(6, 182, 212, 0.45)`).\n  * **Legal Moves**: Center circular dot for quiet moves, target ring for capture squares.\n  * **Last Move**: Soft indigo illumination on source and destination squares.\n  * **Check / Checkmate**: Radial red warning aura directly beneath the endangered king.\n  * **Hint Move**: Emerald green highlight showing Stockfish's recommended move.\n* **Move Validation & Rule Compliance**: Delegated strictly to `chess.js` (castling, en passant, promotions, threefold repetition, 50-move rule, insufficient material, and stalemate).\n* **Interactive Promotion Modal**: Clean glassmorphic overlay to promote pawns to Queen, Rook, Bishop, or Knight.\n* **Live Competitor Cards & Timers**:\n  * **Stockfish AI Card**: Real-time evaluation score, depth indicator, and animated thinking pulse.\n  * **Challenger Card**: 10-minute chess clock with low-time alert (<30s).\n* **Right Panel Information**:\n  * **Engine Telemetry**: Live depth, centipawn evaluation score, nodes per second (NPS), and principal variation line.\n  * **AI Difficulty Selector**: Preset buttons + custom depth/time sliders.\n  * **Captured Pieces Tray**: Real-time captured piece counts with material differential score (`+1`, `+3`, etc.).\n  * **Move History**: Numbered turns in standard algebraic notation (SAN) with single-click **PGN Export**.\n* **Board Action Controls**:\n  * **New Game**: Clears board, resets timers, and reinitializes engine.\n  * **Undo**: Reverts 2 half-moves against AI so the user regains their turn.\n  * **Hint**: Asks Stockfish to analyze the current position and highlights the best move.\n  * **Flip Board**: Toggles board orientation between White and Black.\n  * **Procedural Sound Engine**: Ultra-low latency Web Audio API synthesizer for move clicks, capture snaps, check alerts, and victory chords (includes Mute toggle).\n  * **Worker Reload**: Fallback control to instantly restart the Stockfish worker if needed.\n\n---\n\n### Verification & Engine Test Results\n\nWe ran automated multi-move simulation tests against the real WebAssembly engine using [test-full-game.cjs](file:///C:/Users/DELL/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/stockfish-chess-arena/test-full-game.cjs):\n\n```text\n=== STARTING STOCKFISH ARENA MULTI-MOVE VALIDATION TEST ===\n[UCI] Engine initialized: uciok\n[UCI] Engine ready: readyok\n[GAME] Starting new game with Stockfish...\n\n[HUMAN] Turn 1: Played e4\n[STOCKFISH] Calculated Best Move: e7e6 (bestmove e7e6 ponder f2f3)\n[VALIDATED LEGAL] Stockfish played: e6\n\n[HUMAN] Turn 2: Played Nf3\n[STOCKFISH] Calculated Best Move: d7d5 (bestmove d7d5 ponder d2d3)\n[VALIDATED LEGAL] Stockfish played: d5\n\n[HUMAN] Turn 3: Played e5\n[STOCKFISH] Calculated Best Move: d5d4 (bestmove d5d4 ponder h2h4)\n[VALIDATED LEGAL] Stockfish played: d4\n\n[HUMAN] Turn 4: Played Nxd4\n[STOCKFISH] Calculated Best Move: d8d4 (bestmove d8d4 ponder d1e2)\n[VALIDATED LEGAL] Stockfish played: Qxd4\n\n[HUMAN] Turn 5: Played a3\n[STOCKFISH] Calculated Best Move: b8d7 (bestmove b8d7 ponder b1c3)\n[VALIDATED LEGAL] Stockfish played: Nd7\n\n====================================================\n🎉 ALL STOCKFISH ENGINE TURNS VERIFIED 100% LEGAL!\n====================================================\nPGN: 1. e4 e6 2. Nf3 d5 3. e5 d4 4. Nxd4 Qxd4 5. a3 Nd7 *\n```\n\n* **Vite Production Build**: Successfully compiled (`dist/assets/index.js` and `dist/assets/index.css`).\n* **Live Dev Server**: Running on `http://localhost:5173/` (HTTP 200 OK verified).\n\n---\n\n### Project Files Reference\n\n- [App.tsx](file:///C:/Users/DELL/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/stockfish-chess-arena/src/App.tsx) — Main layout and arena coordinator\n- [stockfishService.ts](file:///C:/Users/DELL/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/stockfish-chess-arena/src/engine/stockfishService.ts) — Web Worker manager and UCI protocol controller\n- [uciAdapter.ts](file:///C:/Users/DELL/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/stockfish-chess-arena/src/engine/uciAdapter.ts) — UCI command formatter and engine output parser\n- [useChessGame.ts](file:///C:/Users/DELL/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/stockfish-chess-arena/src/hooks/useChessGame.ts) — Core `chess.js` game state, move validator, and clocks\n- [useStockfish.ts](file:///C:/Users/DELL/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/stockfish-chess-arena/src/hooks/useStockfish.ts) — AI turns coordinator and hint generator\n- [ChessboardContainer.tsx](file:///C:/Users/DELL/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/stockfish-chess-arena/src/components/board/ChessboardContainer.tsx) — Responsive board with dynamic highlight overlays\n- [soundEffects.ts](file:///C:/Users/DELL/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/stockfish-chess-arena/src/audio/soundEffects.ts) — Web Audio API procedural sound engine\n\nYou can open `http://localhost:5173/` in your browser to play against Stockfish.","thinking":"Both the main application and the Stockfish JavaScript file are accessible, confirmed by the HTTP 200 OK status codes. The successful retrieval of both indicates the web server is correctly serving the necessary files for the application. The architecture incorporates a dedicated Web Worker to execute the Stockfish engine off the main thread, and uses the UCI protocol.\n\n\nThe application uses the Universal Chess Interface (UCI) protocol to communicate with the Stockfish engine. It parses real-time UCI responses, extracting move information and evaluation metrics. The `chess.js` engine validates moves, handles game states, and implements rules such as pawn promotion and captured piece tracking, alongside player chess clocks.\n\n\n"}
{"step_index":244,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-24T07:26:45Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nNow implement advanced chess gameplay features.\n\nFEATURES:\n\n1. Undo Move: Undo the player's and AI's last moves correctly.\n2. Hint: Ask Stockfish to calculate and suggest the best move without changing the game position.\n3. Move History: Display moves in standard algebraic notation.\n4. Board Flip: Allow players to flip the chessboard.\n5. New Game: Reset the game and engine state.\n6. Difficulty: Allow changing AI difficulty before starting a new game.\n7. Timer: Implement configurable chess clocks.\n8. Captured Pieces: Display captured pieces for both players.\n9. Game Results: Detect checkmate, stalemate, and draws.\n10. Promotion: Allow the user to select a promotion piece.\n\nKeep the engine and chess game state synchronized at all times.\n\nTest each feature individually.\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-11-24T12:26:45+05:00.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
{"step_index":245,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-24T07:26:47Z","model":"gemini-3.8-flash-high","input_tokens":121323,"cache_read_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1592,"thinking":"Initial focus is on implementing the requested advanced gameplay features in chess. The features include undo move, hints, move history display, board flip, new game reset, and difficulty adjustment. Planning to approach each feature individually, starting with undo move functionality.\n\n\nExamining the codebase, several components require enhancement to implement the advanced gameplay features. Identifying hooks and UI components related to the chess game state, Stockfish integration, board display, and user controls. Focus on enhancing existing components like `useChessGame.ts`, `ChessboardContainer.tsx`, `PromotionModal.tsx`, and `BoardControls.tsx` to add functionality for undo move, captured pieces, game results, and promotion selection. The initial focus is on the undo move feature implementation.\n\n\nUndo functionality requires special handling when the AI is processing, mandating the engine stop and cancellation of any pending move updates before reverting turns. The feature also must handle scenarios like game-over states, allowing the game to continue after an undo. The engine position synchronization is crucial, which could be done via `ucinewgame` or `position fen`.\n\nConsidering the \"Hint\" feature, the hint calculation must be canceled if a user move occurs simultaneously, ensuring the hint is relevant to the current board state. The UI will show a more dynamic hint with animated indicators on source and destination squares and a textual suggestion in standard chess notation.\n\nThe move history implementation will display the moves in standard algebraic notation (SAN), with optional interactive navigation and PGN export functionality. A board flip feature will enable perspective changes.\n\n\nConsidering color selection for new games, if the player chooses black, the engine needs to initiate a move as white. The new game feature necessitates resetting the board state, clocks, history, and engine state, including running `ucinewgame` and handling the initial move for black. Difficulty levels will be configurable via a `Skill Level` UCI setting. Time control options will range from bullet to custom settings, with proper turn switching and timeout detection. The display will include captured pieces and material differences, along with game result detection for various ending conditions.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"update_focus","args":{"focus":"Inspecting active tasks and current codebase state"}},{"name":"manage_task","args":{"Action":"list"}}]}
